---
title: Pirozhki
description: Puff pastry meat pies
servings: 8
yield: 24
cook time: 45 minutes
prep time: 50 minutes
cuisine: Russian
---

== Meat Filling ==

In a #skillet heat half the @butter{6%tbs}(used in two parts), then add
@lean ground beef{1/2%lb} and cook until brown.

Remove the meat from the pan and grind (again). A #stand mixer{} with a
#grinder attachment{} works well.

Add @water or broth{3/4%c} to the skillet and heat while scraping loose any
browned particles.

In #another skillet{} heat the rest of the butter, add @onion{2}(chopped)
and cook until brown.

Stir in @flour{2%tbs}. Add the liquid from the first skillet and cook,
stirring, until thick.

Mix in the twice ground beef, @salt{1%tsp}, @fresh parsley{2%tbs}(chopped,
or substitute powdered dill to taste), and @black pepper{}(to taste) and
season to taste.

== Assembly ==

Roll @puff pastry dough{}(Pepperidge Farm is convenient) to less than 1/4"
thickness and cut into in 3"x3" or 4"x4" squares.

Wet the edges of a square. Place a rounded teaspoon of meat filling in the
center of the square. Fold one corner of the dough square to the opposite
corner, seal the edges, and roll into a long shape with tapering ends and a
plump center. Turn the tapered ends toward each other into a sort of crab
shape.

Preheat #oven to 425°F .

Place filled and sealed pies on a #baking sheet{}(greased), cover and let
stand until the dough is light, about ~{20 minutes}.

Brush the tops with egg yolk mixture (@egg yolk{1} and @water{1%tbs}) and
bake at 425°F for ~{15 minutes}. Lower the oven temperature to 400°F and
bake until brown, about ~{20 minutes} more.

Serve warm accompanying @./borscht{} or on their own. Reheat in an oven,
not microwave.

